            <ArticleTitle>Gastrointestinal emergencies in the acquired immunodeficiency syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>409-18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opportunistic infection and neoplasia involving the gastrointestinal tract are common in AIDS patients. Life-threatening complications of this involvement may occur, requiring urgent diagnosis and therapy. We review the clinical presentation and approaches to management of AIDS-related gastrointestinal emergencies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
